{"skill":{"slug":"paddleocr-doc-parsing","displayName":"PaddleOCR Document Parsing"},"version":{"version":"3.0.0","createdAt":1780654301609,"changelog":"- Significant update: migrated from custom scripts and detailed workflow to usage of the official PaddleOCR CLI.\n- Removed all helper scripts and schema/reference files.\n- Updated instructions for document parsing using the new paddleocr api command-line interface.\n- Simplified configuration: only requires PADDLEOCR_ACCESS_TOKEN and paddleocr CLI.\n- Added quick-start usage examples with key CLI options and new output format.\n- Clarified error handling and preprocessing recommendations.","changelogSource":"user","license":"MIT-0","files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3892,"sha256":"16f943b1e47f317e8c73ae33bacd63cbc872190baac6a86a868bcbac9b8815c0","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2295,"sha256":"8c20659d80fe614b18172f44afc929f514c80839734a2b03c4f6631b13378bd5","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"clean","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789034074502,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"6ed8fb51276387d6e6ca0c51d20639df5afe9013b468ed72357a7d053f415605","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/6ed8fb51276387d6e6ca0c51d20639df5afe9013b468ed72357a7d053f415605","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":null,"normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":null,"source":"engines","checkedAt":1780658209730},"skillspector":{"status":"clean","normalizedStatus":"clean","score":0,"severity":"LOW","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":0,"checkedAt":1789034074502},"llm":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill coherently installs and uses PaddleOCR to parse documents, with no artifact evidence of hidden behavior or malicious actions.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Requiring PADDLEOCR_ACCESS_TOKEN is proportionate for the PaddleOCR API, but users should expect submitted documents and output resources to be handled by that external service.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The skill installs the third-party paddleocr executable via uv without a pinned version, which is expected for the purpose but leaves normal supply-chain update risk.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"note"},{"detail":"Runtime instructions are limited to user-supplied local files or URLs and documented PaddleOCR options; they do not request agent role changes, memory writes, broad local indexing, or unrelated data access.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The artifact contains no persistence mechanism, background worker, privilege escalation, tool hijacking, scheduled task, or bundled executable script.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is document parsing/OCR, and the instructions only show PaddleOCR CLI use for PDFs, images, tables, formulas, layouts, page ranges, and result output.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"ok"}],"guidance":"Install this only if you are comfortable using PaddleOCR and providing a PaddleOCR access token. Avoid processing highly sensitive documents unless the PaddleOCR service terms and your environment controls are acceptable, and prefer a pinned or reviewed package version where possible.","findings":"[T08] expected: The scan flagged an unpinned executable third-party dependency. Installing PaddleOCR is purpose-aligned, and the artifact contains no malicious code or persistence, so this is dependency hygiene guidance rather than a Review-level concern.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789034074502}}}}}